%% DM26-0670

%% A client comes back after its connection dropped, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md and
%% cassini-client-reliability.md). A registration id is not a bearer token: only its identity and instance may resume it.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Agent (a new transport, under its facade)
    participant Listener as new Listener
    participant SM as SessionManager
    participant SA as SessionAgent (detached)
    participant Subs as SubscriberManager / SubscriberAgents

    Note over Client,Subs: The old connection hit EOF or an I/O error: its session is detached for the retention window,<br/>and its subscribers keep what they hold while the budget allows.
    Client->>Listener: TCP connect, mutual TLS, identity and instance from the leaf
    Client->>Listener: RegistrationRequest(protocol, the old registration_id)
    Note over Listener: Refused first if the protocol differs or the certificate is revoked (broker/client_registration).
    Listener->>SM: RegistrationRequest(client_id, registration_id, identity, instance)

    alt the session is held, not superseded, and this identity and instance may resume it
        SM->>SA: ReassignClient(this Listener)
        SM-->>Listener: RegistrationResponse(Ok the same id, the session's address)
        Listener->>SA: ConnectionOpened
        Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Ok)
        SM->>Subs: RegistrationRequest(id): replay what is held
        Note over SM,Subs: Told only once the session has the new connection: told sooner,<br/>they replayed to the dead one.
        Subs->>Listener: each delivery not acknowledged, oldest first, with the number it had
        Listener-->>Client: PublishResponse(delivery_id) (at-least-once: one it had may come twice)
        Listener->>Subs: SubscriptionsOf(id), to judge them under this certificate
        opt one is no longer allowed
            Listener-->>Client: SubscribeAcknowledgment(Err reason), and it is dropped
        end
    else it was ended early, its budget exhausted while it was away
        SM-->>Listener: SessionEnded(id, why)
        Listener-->>Client: SessionEnded(id, why)
        Client->>Client: ClientEvent::SessionEnded, the agent resynchronises
        SM-->>Listener: RegistrationResponse(Ok a new id)
        Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Ok, a new id)
    else the retention passed, it never existed, or another identity asks
        SM-->>Listener: RegistrationResponse(Ok a new id)
        Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Ok, a new id)
    else it was superseded: this instance lost it and is still running
        SM-->>Listener: RegistrationResponse(Ok a new id), which supersedes nothing
        Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse(Ok, a new id)
        Note over SM: Two live instances do not take turns closing each other.
    end
    Client->>Client: ClientEvent::Registered: subscriptions sent again, each decided at the Listener
    Client->>Listener: the facade sends its whole outbox again, in order, with the numbers it had
